{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-341457",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x-1)] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x-1)] \\\\  & =3\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+(x-1)^{2}}}]\\cdot (x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+({x}^{2}-2x+1)}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|x-1|}\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
